1
00:00:00,332 --> 00:00:01,281
Grid Bot Builder.

2
00:00:01,819 --> 00:00:02,880
Grid Bot Blueprint.

3
00:00:03,340 --> 00:00:04,074
Lesson one.

4
00:00:04,626 --> 00:00:05,355
Introduction.

5
00:00:06,470 --> 00:00:07,616
Education only.

6
00:00:08,175 --> 00:00:09,489
Not financial advice.

7
00:00:10,009 --> 00:00:12,061
This is general information and

8
00:00:12,061 --> 00:00:14,264
doesn't consider your objectives,

9
00:00:14,264 --> 00:00:16,164
financial situation or needs.

10
00:00:16,684 --> 00:00:18,002
Crypto is high risk.

11
00:00:18,522 --> 00:00:20,757
You could lose all the money you put in.

12
00:00:21,467 --> 00:00:23,583
Crypto carries a risk of total loss.

13
00:00:24,783 --> 00:00:26,839
The prices are public historical

14
00:00:26,839 --> 00:00:28,601
daily closes, marked Example.

15
00:00:29,121 --> 00:00:31,188
A close is the last price of the day.

16
00:00:32,343 --> 00:00:34,408
Past performance is not a reliable

17
00:00:34,408 --> 00:00:36,117
indicator of future results.

18
00:00:37,317 --> 00:00:39,682
A grid bot places waiting buy orders

19
00:00:39,682 --> 00:00:41,810
on lines below the price and sell

20
00:00:41,810 --> 00:00:43,939
orders on lines above it, inside a

21
00:00:43,939 --> 00:00:45,673
top and a bottom you choose.

22
00:00:46,193 --> 00:00:47,869
The space between your top and

23
00:00:47,869 --> 00:00:49,600
your bottom is called the band.

24
00:00:50,390 --> 00:00:52,096
A limit order is an order that

25
00:00:52,096 --> 00:00:53,660
waits at a price you choose.

26
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:55,744
It does not chase the price.

27
00:00:56,163 --> 00:00:57,727
Chasing the price would mean

28
00:00:57,727 --> 00:00:59,180
moving the order to follow

29
00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:00,744
wherever the price has gone.

30
00:01:01,743 --> 00:01:03,923
The sells above need some coin, so a

31
00:01:03,923 --> 00:01:06,180
grid starts with part cash and part

32
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:08,359
coin, and that is a description, not

33
00:01:08,359 --> 00:01:09,994
advice about what to hold.

34
00:01:10,514 --> 00:01:12,078
Cash is money you can spend.

35
00:01:12,676 --> 00:01:13,738
Coin is the crypto.

36
00:01:14,829 --> 00:01:16,561
A stop is a rule you write down

37
00:01:16,561 --> 00:01:18,245
before you start, saying what

38
00:01:18,245 --> 00:01:20,024
you will do if the price leaves

39
00:01:20,024 --> 00:01:21,812
the band and does not come back.

40
00:01:23,004 --> 00:01:24,850
When a chart says Example, it

41
00:01:24,850 --> 00:01:26,696
means a real past price used

42
00:01:26,696 --> 00:01:28,541
as an example, not a forecast.

43
00:01:29,741 --> 00:01:31,082
By the end you will know

44
00:01:31,082 --> 00:01:32,367
what a grid bot places.

45
00:01:33,496 --> 00:01:35,575
You will see that idea on

46
00:01:35,575 --> 00:01:37,550
one real path from 2023.

47
00:01:38,750 --> 00:01:40,258
You will be able to say the

48
00:01:40,258 --> 00:01:41,711
stop rule in one sentence.

49
00:01:42,665 --> 00:01:44,620
Think of a ladder leaned on a wall.

50
00:01:44,762 --> 00:01:47,108
The rungs wait, and they do not chase you.

51
00:01:47,384 --> 00:01:49,428
The ladder is the analogy, and the

52
00:01:49,428 --> 00:01:51,700
chart beside it is the real past path.

53
00:01:52,750 --> 00:01:54,593
The range is the top line and the

54
00:01:54,593 --> 00:01:56,437
bottom line, taken from the path.

55
00:01:56,916 --> 00:01:58,368
Every close in this window

56
00:01:58,368 --> 00:02:00,100
stayed between those two lines.

57
00:02:00,886 --> 00:02:02,725
The range is a top and a bottom

58
00:02:02,725 --> 00:02:04,258
you draw before any rung.

59
00:02:04,778 --> 00:02:06,287
Without a top and a bottom,

60
00:02:06,287 --> 00:02:07,739
you can't place the lines.

61
00:02:08,801 --> 00:02:11,393
Six equal gaps of about 900 dollars sit

62
00:02:11,393 --> 00:02:14,066
between the bottom line and the top line.

63
00:02:14,586 --> 00:02:17,326
The about 900 dollar gap is the step from

64
00:02:17,326 --> 00:02:19,818
one line to the next, worked out as the

65
00:02:19,818 --> 00:02:22,641
top line minus the bottom line divided by

66
00:02:22,641 --> 00:02:24,717
the six gaps, not the whole band.

67
00:02:25,237 --> 00:02:27,076
Seven lines make those six gaps.

68
00:02:27,596 --> 00:02:29,328
A limit order waits on a level.

69
00:02:29,684 --> 00:02:31,472
It does not run after the price.

70
00:02:32,395 --> 00:02:33,903
The levels are limit orders

71
00:02:33,903 --> 00:02:35,188
that wait on the rungs.

72
00:02:35,506 --> 00:02:37,182
A limit order sits at a price.

73
00:02:37,684 --> 00:02:38,718
It does not chase.

74
00:02:39,918 --> 00:02:42,246
A fence has a top rail and a bottom rail.

75
00:02:42,766 --> 00:02:44,717
Inside them, the price can wander.

76
00:02:45,237 --> 00:02:47,059
On the chart those rails are the

77
00:02:47,059 --> 00:02:48,679
bottom line and the top line.

78
00:02:49,721 --> 00:02:50,950
The daily close is the

79
00:02:50,950 --> 00:02:52,179
last price of the day.

80
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:54,400
Crypto trades all day, so the

81
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:55,808
day is cut at a set time.

82
00:02:56,328 --> 00:02:58,312
This is a simple candle that shows

83
00:02:58,312 --> 00:02:59,988
the day's high, low and close.

84
00:03:00,469 --> 00:03:03,648
This candle is 19 July 2023.

85
00:03:04,168 --> 00:03:05,397
The high, the low, and

86
00:03:05,397 --> 00:03:06,682
the close are labelled.

87
00:03:07,575 --> 00:03:09,704
The example is Bitcoin's public

88
00:03:09,704 --> 00:03:11,360
daily price in US dollars.

89
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:15,079
From 19 July 2023 to 16 October

90
00:03:15,079 --> 00:03:18,022
2023, every one of those days

91
00:03:18,022 --> 00:03:20,453
closed inside the band.

92
00:03:20,973 --> 00:03:22,761
We do not need to read each day.

93
00:03:23,027 --> 00:03:24,370
The shape is the lesson,

94
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:25,783
and it is marked Example.

95
00:03:26,833 --> 00:03:28,565
A stop is a rule you write down

96
00:03:28,565 --> 00:03:30,250
before you start, saying what

97
00:03:30,250 --> 00:03:32,029
you will do if the price leaves

98
00:03:32,029 --> 00:03:33,817
the band and does not come back.

99
00:03:34,328 --> 00:03:36,757
On 23 October 2023 the close

100
00:03:36,757 --> 00:03:39,185
finished above the top line.

101
00:03:39,705 --> 00:03:41,269
The price did not come back,

102
00:03:41,269 --> 00:03:42,889
so this example was finished.

103
00:03:43,695 --> 00:03:44,813
Write your stop rule

104
00:03:44,813 --> 00:03:46,042
down before you start.

105
00:03:46,337 --> 00:03:48,958
On the card it says: Stop = when you quit.

106
00:03:50,158 --> 00:03:52,914
Worked check: 19 July

107
00:03:52,914 --> 00:03:55,995
2023 to 16 October 2023.

108
00:03:56,515 --> 00:03:59,187
Six equal gaps of about 900 dollars.

109
00:03:59,707 --> 00:04:01,216
The low is the bottom line.

110
00:04:01,696 --> 00:04:03,162
The high is the top line.

111
00:04:04,212 --> 00:04:06,293
The stop rule is: if the daily close

112
00:04:06,293 --> 00:04:08,226
leaves the top line and does not

113
00:04:08,226 --> 00:04:10,084
come back, the idea is finished.

114
00:04:10,604 --> 00:04:12,447
Nothing on this card is an order.

115
00:04:13,411 --> 00:04:15,021
Price often moves sideways,

116
00:04:15,021 --> 00:04:16,772
bouncing between the same top

117
00:04:16,772 --> 00:04:18,522
and bottom instead of leaving.

118
00:04:19,042 --> 00:04:20,620
A grid is a ladder of limit

119
00:04:20,620 --> 00:04:22,573
orders built for that bouncing.

120
00:04:23,093 --> 00:04:24,949
When price runs one way and stays

121
00:04:24,949 --> 00:04:27,072
there, the bot has nothing left to do.

122
00:04:28,142 --> 00:04:30,183
A grid has three parts you can name:

123
00:04:30,183 --> 00:04:32,194
the range, the levels, and the stop.

124
00:04:32,670 --> 00:04:33,900
The range is the band.

125
00:04:34,410 --> 00:04:36,366
The levels are the rungs inside it.

126
00:04:37,415 --> 00:04:39,829
Buy orders sit on lines below the price

127
00:04:39,829 --> 00:04:42,093
and sell orders sit on lines above it.

128
00:04:42,613 --> 00:04:44,752
The sells need some coin, so a grid

129
00:04:44,752 --> 00:04:47,049
starts with part cash and part coin,

130
00:04:47,049 --> 00:04:49,425
and that is a description, not advice.

131
00:04:50,625 --> 00:04:52,525
No order is sent from this lesson.

132
00:04:52,855 --> 00:04:53,865
You draw the idea.

133
00:04:54,385 --> 00:04:56,179
If a screen appears later, it

134
00:04:56,179 --> 00:04:57,894
should be a copy of the page,

135
00:04:57,894 --> 00:04:59,454
and only on paper or demo.

136
00:05:00,654 --> 00:05:02,274
The course is a map, and this

137
00:05:02,274 --> 00:05:04,397
